  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Dark Workbench",
    "overview": "DiffSlice is a polished dark developer workbench: graphite surfaces, bright readable ink, blue actions, fine rules, and a split-square brand mark. Its code atlas uses the familiar geometry of a disk analyzer, with restrained categorical rectangles and explicit comparison colors that make source size and change status legible at a glance.\n\nThe main surface stays calm and spatial; supporting controls and the changed-file tree are compact. Source comparison appears when a changed file is selected, preserving map context above it. This is a code-led system; the implemented viewer is the authority for measurements and states.",
